<Article title="Privacy" description="How this portfolio handles your visit, browser preferences, and messages." canonicalPath="/privacy-policy.html" eyebrow="Updated October 11, 2026">
<p>This is Chris Mackintosh’s personal portfolio. This notice describes this version of the website.</p>
<h2>Browsing this site</h2>
<p>This site does not include advertising, analytics scripts, session recording, tracking pixels, account registration, or contact forms. Fonts and portfolio images are served with the site. The site’s own code does not set cookies.</p>
<p>The hosting service processes technical request information, such as your IP address, the requested URL, and browser information, to deliver and protect the site. This is separate from advertising or visitor analytics. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub states that it logs visitors’ IP addresses for security purposes. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection">GitHub Pages data collection</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p>
<h2>Preferences in your browser</h2>
<p>The site uses local storage to remember your light or dark appearance preference (<code>cm-color-appearance</code>). Session storage remembers your position when you open a project and return to the homepage. Local storage also caches a recent Denver weather observation and its retrieval time for up to 15 minutes of reuse. The cached entry may remain in browser storage until replaced or cleared, but expired observations are not used. These stored values stay in your browser; the site does not send them to me.</p>
<p>You can clear this information through your browser’s site-data controls. Persistent preferences remain until you clear them; session information normally ends when the tab’s browsing session ends. The site remains readable if browser storage or JavaScript is disabled.</p>
<h2>The sky animation</h2>
<p>The sky combines a local sunrise and sunset calculation for Denver with recent National Weather Service (NWS) observations from Denver International Airport. It does not request or use your location.
</p><p>When a cached observation is unavailable or due for refresh, each open page requests weather from <code>api.weather.gov</code>, at most once every 15 minutes while the page is visible. NWS receives your IP address and normal browser request information. The request does not include cookies, credentials, or a referring-page address. See <a href="https://www.weather.gov/privacy">NWS privacy information</a>.
</p><p>If the request fails or the observation is too old, the sky falls back to the local daylight calculation. The animation is a decorative interpretation of weather, not an official NWS weather product.</p>
<h2>If you email me</h2>
<p>Email links open your email application. If you send a message, I receive the address and information you choose to share and use them to respond and manage our correspondence. Please avoid sending sensitive information you do not want included in an email.</p>
<h2>Links to other websites</h2>
<p>Social profiles, project sources, and other external links take you to services with their own privacy practices. External content is linked rather than embedded.</p>
<h2>Questions and updates</h2>
<p>For privacy questions or requests about information you have emailed me, contact <a href="mailto:hello@chrismackintosh.work">hello@chrismackintosh.work</a>. If this site’s data practices change, this page and its update date will change too.</p>
</Article>
